From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:34:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Reserve the SCP
 firmware memory

The boot chain loads the firmware of the SCP, the A733's management core,
to DRAM at 0x48100000 and leaves it running, but does not reserve that
memory. Reserve 1 MiB there as no-map, so the kernel neither uses nor maps
it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the kernel reserves
0x48100000-0x481fffff as no-map, and /proc/iomem lists it as reserved.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts     | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 3cb3060ed566..854896c0fb2c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -24,6 +24,18 @@ ext_osc32k: ext-osc32k-clk {
 		clock-output-names = "ext_osc32k";
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/* SCP firmware, loaded and left running by the boot chain */
+		scp@48100000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x48100000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	reg_vcc3v3: vcc3v3 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vcc-3v3";
